---
title: Paper Mario DX
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Paper Mario DX is a modified version of the Paper Mario [decompilation](https://papermar.io) specifically tailored for making mods.

## Requirements

You will need:

- A computer running Windows 10+, macOS, or Linux
- The [Paper Mario (US) ROM](https://dumping.guide/carts/nintendo/n64#methods) in [.z64](https://hack64.net/tools/swapper.php) format
- [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/) (or a different editor)

## Installation

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="Windows" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. Install [Git for Windows](https://git-scm.com/download/win), keeping all the installer's default options.
  2. Install [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/).
  3. Open VS Code, press **Ctrl+Shift+P** to open the command palette, type `Git: Clone`, and press Enter.
  4. Paste `https://github.com/bates64/papermario-dx.git`, choose a folder to clone into, then click **Open** when VS Code asks whether to open the cloned repository.
  5. Get a Paper Mario (US) ROM in [.z64](https://hack64.net/tools/swapper.php) format, rename it to `baserom.z64`, and put it in the `ver/us` folder inside the project.
  6. Press **Ctrl+Shift+B** to build the game. The first build downloads the compiler toolchain, so it takes longer than later builds.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="macOS" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. Open Terminal and run `xcode-select --install` to install the Xcode Command Line Tools, which provide `git`. Follow the prompts, then wait for the install to finish.
  2. Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run `brew install ninja python3`.
  3. Run `git clone https://github.com/bates64/papermario-dx.git && cd papermario-dx`.
  4. Get a Paper Mario (US) ROM in [.z64](https://hack64.net/tools/swapper.php) format, rename it to `baserom.z64`, and put it in the `ver/us` folder inside the project.
  5. Install [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/), then open the `papermario-dx` folder you just cloned (**File > Open Folder...**).
  6. Press **Cmd+Shift+B** to build the game. The first build downloads the compiler toolchain, so it takes longer than later builds.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Linux" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. Open a terminal and install `git`, `ninja`, and `python3` using your distribution's package manager, for example on Ubuntu/Debian: `sudo apt install git ninja-build python3`.
  2. Run `git clone https://github.com/bates64/papermario-dx.git && cd papermario-dx`.
  3. Get a Paper Mario (US) ROM in [.z64](https://hack64.net/tools/swapper.php) format, rename it to `baserom.z64`, and put it in the `ver/us` folder inside the project.
  4. Install [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/), then open the `papermario-dx` folder you just cloned (**File > Open Folder...**).
  5. Press **Ctrl+Shift+B** to build the game. The first build downloads the compiler toolchain, so it takes longer than later builds.
  {% /steps %}
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Nix" %}
  {% steps %}
  1. Install [Nix](https://nixos.org/download), using the default (multi-user) installer options.
  2. Get a Paper Mario (US) ROM in [.z64](https://hack64.net/tools/swapper.php) format, rename it to `papermario.us.z64`, then run `nix-store --add-fixed sha256 papermario.us.z64` to add it to the Nix store.
  3. Open a terminal and run `git clone https://github.com/bates64/papermario-dx.git && cd papermario-dx`.
  4. Run `nix --extra-experimental-features "flakes nix-command" develop --profile .nix-profile --accept-flake-config`. This downloads all dependencies and copies the ROM into the project, so it can take a while the first time.
  5. Install [Visual Studio Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/), then run `code .` (still inside the shell from step 4) to open the project.
  {% /steps %}

  Build with **Ctrl+Shift+P > Tasks: Run Task > Build Mod (Nix)** instead of Ctrl+Shift+B, so the build runs inside the Nix environment.
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

## Build and run

With Visual Studio Code focused, **press Ctrl+Shift+B (Cmd+Shift+B on macOS) to build the game.**

The output ROM is located at `ver/us/build/papermario.z64`. Load it in an emulator to play it. We recommend the accurate emulator [ares](https://ares-emu.net). If you don't regularly test with ares and/or real hardware, your mod may not work correctly for others.

If you prefer real hardware, you can copy the output ROM to a flashcart.

## Troubleshooting

If you run into any issues, you can ask for help in the `#papermario-dx` channel in the Star Haven Discord.

### I closed VSCode! How do I open it again?

You can reopen it by using the 'Recent' menu on the VSCode Welcome screen.

If you can't find it, you can open VSCode from a terminal. Open a terminal in your project folder and run `code .`.
